1
00:00:28,140 --> 00:00:29,877
Shattano, Shattano, Shll,
Chess, Chess, Hazz, Chess,

2
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:40,080
Thank you.

3
00:01:08,340 --> 00:01:09,170
Let's go.

4
00:01:30,860 --> 00:01:31,690
Let's go.

5
00:02:59,980 --> 00:03:02,700
Oh, my God.

6
00:03:47,700 --> 00:03:51,520
Are you not feeling
well, Mr. Joe Starr? Yes.

7
00:03:51,820 --> 00:03:53,467
Thank you for asking, Avdol.

8
00:03:53,720 --> 00:03:56,877
I've had some bad experiences
with planes in the past.

9
00:03:56,960 --> 00:03:58,480
As I mentioned before,

10
00:03:58,740 --> 00:04:02,900
we have but 50 days to confront Dio,
if we have not succeeded by then.

11
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:07,260
Yes, I understand.

12
00:04:07,680 --> 00:04:10,680
If we cannot make it in
time, then Holly could die.

13
00:04:24,380 --> 00:04:25,210
What?

14
00:04:25,293 --> 00:04:26,123
What was that?

15
00:04:28,620 --> 00:04:31,914
Jostar-san, the engine on the
left side has caught fire.

16
00:04:32,940 --> 00:04:33,780
Calm down.

17
00:04:34,100 --> 00:04:35,453
Everyone remain seated.

18
00:04:36,720 --> 00:04:38,837
But Jostar-san, the engine...

19
00:04:38,920 --> 00:04:39,940
Don't worry.

20
00:04:40,260 --> 00:04:42,672
I'll go ask the pilots about this myself.

21
00:04:48,440 --> 00:04:50,897
Captain, please tell me
what's happening here.

22
00:04:50,980 --> 00:04:52,297
I'm trying to find out.

23
00:04:52,380 --> 00:04:54,145
We're rapidly losing altitude.

24
00:04:54,580 --> 00:04:55,577
We're out of control.

25
00:04:55,660 --> 00:04:57,542
You have to return to your seat.

26
00:04:57,740 --> 00:05:00,317
Unless we regain control, we're
going to crash into the ocean.

27
00:05:00,400 --> 00:05:02,000
What did you say?

28
00:05:08,800 --> 00:05:09,980
What a pain.

29
00:05:39,420 --> 00:05:42,297
The important thing is
that everyone is all right.

30
00:05:42,380 --> 00:05:44,674
Many ships travel through these waters.

31
00:05:44,860 --> 00:05:48,017
They'll pick up our distress signal
and surely come to our rescue.

32
00:05:48,100 --> 00:05:49,897
I sure hope you're right about that.

33
00:05:49,980 --> 00:05:52,957
We certainly can't afford to hang
around in a place like this for long.

34
00:05:53,040 --> 00:05:56,500
But I wonder, could our enemies
have caused this accident?

35
00:06:04,460 --> 00:06:05,290
Huh?

36
00:06:06,840 --> 00:06:10,664
Hmm, my friends, it seems that
our luck has not run out just yet.

37
00:06:11,200 --> 00:06:12,030
Huh?

38
00:06:19,120 --> 00:06:20,260
Please signal them.

39
00:06:51,960 --> 00:06:53,697
Right then, now we can go back.

40
00:06:53,780 --> 00:06:57,427
Guess we shouldn't take my natural
good luck too lightly, huh?

41
00:07:00,240 --> 00:07:02,480
Is something bothering you, Avdolsan?

42
00:07:02,740 --> 00:07:04,677
The ramp has already been lowered for us,

43
00:07:04,760 --> 00:07:08,172
but why aren't any of the crew
members showing themselves?

44
00:07:39,860 --> 00:07:41,540
No one's coming to meet us.

45
00:07:42,660 --> 00:07:45,013
Just where the hell is the crew, anyway?

46
00:07:45,300 --> 00:07:48,580
Just like that famous abandoned
ship, the Mary Celeste.

47
00:07:50,480 --> 00:07:51,310
Hey!

48
00:07:51,393 --> 00:07:52,440
Is there anyone here?

49
00:07:53,020 --> 00:07:54,220
Anyone here?

50
00:07:54,660 --> 00:07:55,860
Anyone here?

51
00:07:58,020 --> 00:07:59,255
Is there anyone here?

52
00:07:59,840 --> 00:08:02,020
He's here! He's here!

53
00:08:02,180 --> 00:08:03,040
He's here!

54
00:08:03,180 --> 00:08:05,000
He's here! He's here!

55
00:08:06,520 --> 00:08:08,873
In any case, let's investigate the ship.

56
00:08:24,200 --> 00:08:25,318
Is something wrong?

57
00:08:28,660 --> 00:08:29,797
Look at this window.

58
00:08:29,880 --> 00:08:33,762
How could they have spotted us
through a window as filthy as that?

59
00:08:41,680 --> 00:08:44,798
It appears there is no one
in the engine room either.

60
00:08:51,400 --> 00:08:56,020
So there's no one on board
what was that just now?

61
00:08:58,420 --> 00:09:01,780
Josa what is it there
was a sound from inside!

62
00:09:15,300 --> 00:09:17,040
What a gigantic monkey.

63
00:09:21,240 --> 00:09:23,200
This appears to be an orangutan.

64
00:09:29,120 --> 00:09:30,977
Is he telling us to open the cage?

65
00:09:31,060 --> 00:09:32,825
Certainly looks like it to me.

66
00:09:42,280 --> 00:09:44,860
Oh, you're a pretty
smart guy for a monkey.

67
00:09:45,240 --> 00:09:46,320
Please be careful.

68
00:09:46,560 --> 00:09:49,297
An orangutan is five times
stronger than a human,

69
00:09:49,380 --> 00:09:51,498
so he could easily rip your arm off.

70
00:09:53,220 --> 00:09:54,400
He's not starving,

71
00:09:54,680 --> 00:09:58,915
which means there's at least one
person on board who's been feeding him.

72
00:09:59,840 --> 00:10:00,670
Right, then.

73
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:02,412
Let's go find the owner.

74
00:10:13,220 --> 00:10:14,050
Hmm?

75
00:10:19,460 --> 00:10:20,290
What the?

76
00:10:29,740 --> 00:10:32,100
Hmm, look up there, on the bridge.

77
00:10:40,300 --> 00:10:41,130
Hmm?

78
00:10:44,780 --> 00:10:47,820
This is a ghost ship. Ridiculous.

79
00:11:00,960 --> 00:11:03,842
I think it would be best
if we all stay together.

80
00:11:07,060 --> 00:11:07,917
What do you think?

81
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:08,830
Anyone?

82
00:11:09,400 --> 00:11:10,988
This ship is too dangerous.

83
00:11:11,200 --> 00:11:13,906
What can we do now in
the middle of the ocean?

84
00:11:14,180 --> 00:11:17,004
But we're not sure where
the ship is headed yet.

85
00:11:21,400 --> 00:11:22,230
What's that?

86
00:11:25,040 --> 00:11:26,746
I guess we'll have to go see.

87
00:11:27,380 --> 00:11:28,210
Hmm.

88
00:11:59,120 --> 00:12:00,760
Bonjour, Monsieur Joestar.

89
00:12:01,040 --> 00:12:02,452
Greetings to your party.

90
00:12:04,120 --> 00:12:05,700
Ah, you! Wait.

91
00:12:09,640 --> 00:12:12,040
Tell me, how is it you know about us?

92
00:12:15,860 --> 00:12:19,080
A man with a birthmark
shaped like this told me.

93
00:12:24,280 --> 00:12:25,580
You're one of them.

94
00:12:29,460 --> 00:12:31,260
Justice! Look out!

95
00:12:33,560 --> 00:12:34,400
What?

96
00:12:45,340 --> 00:12:46,180
What?

97
00:12:47,920 --> 00:12:51,660
My Stan's name is Silver Chariot.

98
00:12:51,960 --> 00:12:55,600
So, Avdol, it would appear that
you are very anxious to die.

99
00:12:58,180 --> 00:13:01,080
I made a clock out of fire on that table.

100
00:13:01,460 --> 00:13:04,940
Before it burns 12 o
'clock, I will kill you.

101
00:13:05,160 --> 00:13:07,219
That was very formidable swordplay.

102
00:13:07,380 --> 00:13:08,439
I am truly in awe.

103
00:13:09,240 --> 00:13:11,637
But you say you would
kill me by 12 o 'clock.

104
00:13:11,720 --> 00:13:12,550
Well,

105
00:13:12,633 --> 00:13:16,947
don't you think that you are being just
a little bit too vain, man from France?

106
00:13:17,380 --> 00:13:19,040
My greeting is overdue.

107
00:13:19,320 --> 00:13:21,417
Please allow me to introduce myself.

108
00:13:21,500 --> 00:13:25,960
My name is Polnareff,
Jean-Pierre Polnareff.

109
00:13:27,500 --> 00:13:28,397
Merci beaucoup.

110
00:13:28,480 --> 00:13:30,757
My sincere thanks for your introduction.

111
00:13:30,840 --> 00:13:31,700
Now that...

112
00:13:33,140 --> 00:13:35,597
All Avdol's stand did was move its arm,

113
00:13:35,680 --> 00:13:38,337
and the lower half of the
table has burned away.

114
00:13:38,420 --> 00:13:40,957
It is very important that you realize my

115
00:13:41,040 --> 00:13:43,740
stand's fire is not like
some ordinary flame.

116
00:13:43,980 --> 00:13:48,540
And because my stand can control fire
at will, it is called Magician's Red.

117
00:13:49,680 --> 00:13:50,800
Hmm. Impressive.

118
00:13:51,340 --> 00:13:54,520
But a while ago, you said I was too vain.

119
00:13:55,140 --> 00:13:57,860
You think I'm vain about
my swordplay skill?

120
00:14:03,080 --> 00:14:04,660
Too vain, you said?

121
00:14:04,980 --> 00:14:06,860
Can you still say that now?

122
00:14:08,900 --> 00:14:09,730
Amazing.

123
00:14:09,813 --> 00:14:12,896
He was able to pierce five
coins with a single thrust.

124
00:14:13,060 --> 00:14:14,857
No, there's more to it than that.

125
00:14:14,940 --> 00:14:16,881
Take another look at those coins.

126
00:14:19,300 --> 00:14:20,740
I see what you mean.

127
00:14:21,700 --> 00:14:24,641
Very good, so you understand
what this means then.

128
00:14:24,880 --> 00:14:28,497
My stand can cut, parry and block
your fire with complete control.

129
00:14:28,580 --> 00:14:33,109
In other words, my friend, this means
you are virtually powerless against me.

130
00:14:35,520 --> 00:14:36,740
When did he...?

131
00:14:40,860 --> 00:14:43,180
Avdol, I could kill you here and now,

132
00:14:43,320 --> 00:14:45,697
but the size of this room
put you at a disadvantage.

133
00:14:45,780 --> 00:14:50,057
A more open space would allow you to
use your ability at full power, right?

134
00:14:50,140 --> 00:14:53,357
Beating you there would be a more
suitable victory for my stand.

135
00:14:53,440 --> 00:14:54,840
Everyone, get in line.

136
00:14:55,060 --> 00:14:57,472
One by one, I will cut each of you apart.

137
00:15:08,420 --> 00:15:09,820
Well, Avdol, Mr.

138
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:12,529
Joestar, please do not
interfere with this.

139
00:15:12,760 --> 00:15:17,920
Just as he said, with this much open
space, I can more freely use my stand.

140
00:15:18,980 --> 00:15:20,640
I will predict your destiny.

141
00:15:20,940 --> 00:15:25,175
I predict that you will destroy
yourself with your own stance abilities.

142
00:15:33,980 --> 00:15:36,077
What happened to your vaunted flame?

143
00:15:36,160 --> 00:15:39,278
If you're not going to
breathe fire, then I'll start.

144
00:15:50,500 --> 00:15:53,497
That man certainly got a
lot of bloody nerve while he

145
00:15:53,580 --> 00:15:56,639
was just waiting for
Magician's Red to breathe fire.

146
00:15:58,560 --> 00:16:00,720
You don't stand a chance against me.

147
00:16:03,600 --> 00:16:05,820
He's coming for real this time.

148
00:16:10,240 --> 00:16:13,769
By Jove, I wouldn't want to get
broiled by this next attack.

149
00:16:15,260 --> 00:16:16,800
Crossfire coming here!

150
00:16:17,580 --> 00:16:18,410
Hey!

151
00:16:19,440 --> 00:16:21,793
Is that really all the power you've got?

152
00:16:23,160 --> 00:16:24,640
If so...

153
00:16:26,680 --> 00:16:28,820
The stand's flame was too powerful.

154
00:16:29,120 --> 00:16:30,708
It's burning Avdol instead.

155
00:16:31,360 --> 00:16:34,240
Just as I said, right, Monsieur Avdol?

156
00:16:35,260 --> 00:16:38,180
Ah, what a desperate struggle, eh?

157
00:16:40,060 --> 00:16:41,600
What is this resistance?

158
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:46,520
Once again, now, let's fire!

159
00:16:51,400 --> 00:16:52,840
His stand is melting.

160
00:16:53,700 --> 00:16:54,980
He's badly burned.

161
00:16:55,240 --> 00:16:57,475
He's lucky he's only severely injured.

162
00:16:57,680 --> 00:17:00,440
No, perhaps I should say he's unlucky.

163
00:17:00,720 --> 00:17:03,697
In any case, he won't be able
to get up for three months.

164
00:17:03,780 --> 00:17:07,097
His stand has been reduced to
a pulp and is unable to fight.

165
00:17:07,180 --> 00:17:08,010
Well, Mr.

166
00:17:08,093 --> 00:17:12,548
Joestar, we should start talking about
the best way to get to Egypt from here.

167
00:17:16,060 --> 00:17:17,360
Look up there!

168
00:17:18,520 --> 00:17:19,350
What?

169
00:17:22,460 --> 00:17:24,720
I can't believe it.

170
00:17:25,960 --> 00:17:26,790
Bravo!

171
00:17:27,160 --> 00:17:27,990
Bravo!

172
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:33,000
Why is his body floating there in midair?

173
00:17:33,860 --> 00:17:36,820
Look carefully through
the eyes of your stands.

174
00:17:38,640 --> 00:17:40,000
His stand.

175
00:17:43,440 --> 00:17:47,205
Allow me to present Silver Chariot
without his protective armor.

176
00:17:48,860 --> 00:17:51,300
Well, you look appropriately amazed.

177
00:17:51,700 --> 00:17:56,000
If you don't mind, please explain
to me how this is possible. Good.

178
00:17:56,340 --> 00:17:58,340
Your attitude is most commendable.

179
00:17:58,620 --> 00:18:01,817
The explosion earlier was not
my stand being blown to bits,

180
00:18:01,900 --> 00:18:04,841
but the impact of my stand
throwing off his armor.

181
00:18:07,360 --> 00:18:09,654
Only his armor was burned by your fire,

182
00:18:09,760 --> 00:18:12,642
so I was able to get by
with only minor injuries.

183
00:18:13,440 --> 00:18:16,920
And now, with the armor
gone, I can move much faster.

184
00:18:17,220 --> 00:18:19,477
So you're saying that
the weight of your armor

185
00:18:19,560 --> 00:18:22,560
prevented you from avoiding
my crossfire hurricane?

186
00:18:23,640 --> 00:18:25,020
Oui, that is correct.

187
00:18:25,860 --> 00:18:28,297
Which means that without
your protective armor,

188
00:18:28,380 --> 00:18:31,380
you would not survive being
struck by another CFH.

189
00:18:32,300 --> 00:18:35,220
Oui, but that is impossible. Impossible?

190
00:18:36,220 --> 00:18:37,050
Why?

191
00:18:37,133 --> 00:18:40,747
Because I'm about to show you
something that will horrify you.

192
00:18:42,240 --> 00:18:45,297
What the it can't be a person should only

193
00:18:45,380 --> 00:18:49,777
have one stand hmm you
appear to be horrified?

194
00:18:49,860 --> 00:18:53,877
These after images affect not just your
sight but your other senses as well.

195
00:18:53,960 --> 00:18:56,160
How about this sword play now!

196
00:19:01,660 --> 00:19:06,920
That was an after image your stunts
are useless against my stand now!

197
00:19:11,260 --> 00:19:12,090
Avdol!

198
00:19:14,640 --> 00:19:19,700
You should know that I developed a
variation on my crossfire hurricane attack.

199
00:19:19,900 --> 00:19:22,580
The unkshake fire is
normally a single flame,

200
00:19:22,780 --> 00:19:26,192
but I can break it up and hurl
it as many separate flames.

201
00:19:34,300 --> 00:19:35,700
Now really, Avdol!

202
00:19:36,480 --> 00:19:37,380
Not good.

203
00:19:37,620 --> 00:19:39,577
His stands have formed a defensive circle.

204
00:19:39,660 --> 00:19:42,425
He'll strike the flames
back, just like before.

205
00:19:42,940 --> 00:19:44,440
Easy, easy, easy, easy!

206
00:19:49,080 --> 00:19:50,980
I will strike them back.

207
00:19:54,880 --> 00:19:56,000
What the...

208
00:20:03,180 --> 00:20:08,062
That is the hole Polnareff's stand made
earlier when he struck back Avdol's flames.

209
00:20:11,600 --> 00:20:12,880
I get it now.

210
00:20:13,180 --> 00:20:16,520
He made use of a hole created
in the midst of battle.

211
00:20:16,760 --> 00:20:18,917
His ability to split the
flame made it possible

212
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:21,412
for him to pull off this clever strategy.

213
00:20:29,300 --> 00:20:32,359
Burning to death would be
a very painful way to die.

214
00:20:32,640 --> 00:20:35,287
Use that blade and put
an end to your misery.

215
00:20:53,680 --> 00:20:58,800
I was so vain, thinking my swordplay
would never be beaten by mere flames.

216
00:21:00,160 --> 00:21:02,925
For that, I choose to
burn to death gracefully.

217
00:21:03,060 --> 00:21:05,317
Consider this to be a
salute to your abilities

218
00:21:05,400 --> 00:21:07,753
from the one who you defeated in battle.

219
00:21:11,940 --> 00:21:14,580
His proud spirit goes beyond Dio's orders.

220
00:21:14,860 --> 00:21:19,440
This man who remains true to the code
of honor that you call chivalry. Right.

221
00:21:19,740 --> 00:21:22,799
If we let him die like this,
we may regret it later.

222
00:21:23,100 --> 00:21:27,688
Perhaps there's a very good reason why
this man became one of Dio's assassins.

223
00:21:31,300 --> 00:21:32,400
We're safe now.

224
00:21:32,600 --> 00:21:34,247
Our enemy has been defeated.

225
00:21:34,940 --> 00:21:38,137
I have to admit, you really
had me worried for a while.

226
00:21:38,220 --> 00:21:39,050
What a relief.

227
00:21:45,340 --> 00:21:46,400
Hey, watch out!

228
00:21:58,940 --> 00:21:59,920
Hit the deck!

229
00:22:25,620 --> 00:22:27,580
Damn, Ape is a stand user.

230
00:22:32,300 --> 00:22:35,420
He turned that bolt into a pipe. Jotaro!

231
00:22:38,720 --> 00:22:39,550
Chotaro!

232
00:22:39,700 --> 00:22:41,577
This entire ship is his...

233
00:22:41,660 --> 00:22:43,020
His stand!

234
00:22:54,780 --> 00:22:56,020
Hey, monkey.

235
00:22:56,480 --> 00:22:58,040
Your hairy ass is next.

236
00:23:07,800 --> 00:23:09,200
Jotaro!

237
00:23:24,600 --> 00:23:25,430
Jotaro!

238
00:23:55,500 --> 00:23:57,520
It seems to be over now.

239
00:24:01,340 --> 00:24:06,660
But whether this boat will break down
or reach land, Is anyone's guess.

240
00:24:07,100 --> 00:24:11,218
Who would have imagined his stand
made use of a little boat like this?

241
00:24:11,340 --> 00:24:15,987
If we'd known this would happen, maybe
we would have tried to tame that monkey.

242
00:24:18,800 --> 00:24:22,277
He's really something to have recovered
from those injuries so quickly.

243
00:24:22,360 --> 00:24:26,577
There must be something important he
feels he must accomplish in this life.

244
00:24:26,660 --> 00:24:31,601
Otherwise, no matter how young he is, he
would not have been able to heal this fast.

245
00:24:34,180 --> 00:24:35,010
Mr.

246
00:24:35,093 --> 00:24:40,060
Joestar, I may be prying, but I have
noticed that you're always wearing gloves.

247
00:24:40,340 --> 00:24:43,797
Please don't tell me that your
left hand is actually a right hand.

248
00:24:43,880 --> 00:24:45,409
My left hand a right hand?

249
00:24:45,520 --> 00:24:47,960
That is a very peculiar question to ask.

250
00:24:48,160 --> 00:24:52,866
For a long time, I've been searching for
a man whose hands are both right hands.

251
00:24:58,220 --> 00:25:02,100
This is an honorable wound I
received in battle 50 years ago.

252
00:25:02,460 --> 00:25:03,460
My apologies.

253
00:25:03,900 --> 00:25:04,959
Please forgive me.

254
00:25:05,880 --> 00:25:08,897
Polnareff, would you kindly
tell us what this is all about?

255
00:25:08,980 --> 00:25:13,098
I've been looking for the man who
brutally murdered my younger sister.

256
00:25:14,700 --> 00:25:17,200
It happened three years ago.

257
00:25:22,500 --> 00:25:26,980
That day my sister was walking
home from school with a classmate

258
00:26:15,900 --> 00:26:20,260
I don't know his face, but his
hands are both right hands.

259
00:26:21,340 --> 00:26:24,420
Obviously, someone
possessing a stand ability.

260
00:26:26,220 --> 00:26:28,797
I made a vow that he would pay for all the

261
00:26:28,880 --> 00:26:31,762
things he did to my younger
sister with his life.

262
00:26:35,760 --> 00:26:39,580
Then, one year ago, I met Dio.

263
00:26:44,080 --> 00:26:45,940
But, who are you?

264
00:26:47,060 --> 00:26:51,480
I can see a man, boldly
confronting you in your mind.

265
00:26:52,620 --> 00:26:55,740
Listen, how about you
and I become friends?

266
00:26:56,260 --> 00:27:00,500
If you will help me with my
work, I will lend you a hand.

267
00:27:01,260 --> 00:27:03,940
Perhaps I can find that man for you.

268
00:27:05,120 --> 00:27:07,820
So, I was ordered to kill you all,

269
00:27:07,960 --> 00:27:11,195
and even though I knew it
was a whisper from the devil,

270
00:27:11,780 --> 00:27:15,839
I'd made a deal to get the information
I needed to avenge my sisters.

271
00:27:16,420 --> 00:27:17,250
death.

272
00:27:17,333 --> 00:27:20,797
He's very good at finding and taking
advantage of people's weaknesses.

273
00:27:20,880 --> 00:27:22,957
And according to the
story he just told us,

274
00:27:23,040 --> 00:27:26,737
Dio already knew the identity of
the man who killed his sister.

275
00:27:26,820 --> 00:27:27,650
What?

276
00:27:28,680 --> 00:27:31,033
Polnareff, what are you going to do now?

277
00:27:31,720 --> 00:27:34,896
I'd like to join you guys
on your mission to find Dio.

278
00:27:35,040 --> 00:27:38,864
If I go after him too, I might
meet the man who killed my sister.

279
00:27:39,340 --> 00:27:40,780
A jolly good idea.

280
00:27:41,060 --> 00:27:44,589
Our goals may be different, but
our destination is the same.

281
00:27:45,700 --> 00:27:46,740
All right, then.

282
00:27:46,940 --> 00:27:49,577
Let's stop messing around
and get our butts to Egypt.

283
00:27:49,660 --> 00:27:51,217
This is going to be a blast.

284
00:27:51,300 --> 00:27:56,006
Oh, those Egyptian women are so mysterious
and appealing that I can hardly wait.

285
00:27:56,620 --> 00:28:00,137
I thought he was a man who lived
by a code of honor and chivalry,

286
00:28:00,220 --> 00:28:01,632
but now I'm not so sure.

287
00:28:02,020 --> 00:28:04,255
His mood certainly changes in a hurry.

288
00:28:04,800 --> 00:28:08,388
His mind and his instincts seem
to be completely independent.

289
00:28:10,620 --> 00:28:11,900
Oh, what a pain.

290
00:28:23,760 --> 00:28:24,590
Strength.

291
00:28:24,673 --> 00:28:25,960
So useless.

292
00:28:26,760 --> 00:28:31,660
Not only that, even the chariot
Polnareff double-crossed us.

293
00:28:33,280 --> 00:28:37,520
However, all the cards of
destiny still remain in my hands.

294
00:28:40,960 --> 00:28:43,857
Don't allow this to trouble you, Lord Dio.

295
00:28:43,940 --> 00:28:47,780
No matter how many of those
useless worms defect to the enemy,

296
00:28:48,060 --> 00:28:50,472
they can never be a match for your power.

297
00:28:50,640 --> 00:28:55,520
Besides that, the Emperor and the Hanged
Man are already on their way to India.

298
00:28:56,280 --> 00:28:57,840
One of them will do it.

299
00:28:58,180 --> 00:29:01,768
The Hanged Man's right hands
will take care of them for sure.

300
00:29:04,020 --> 00:29:07,040
Because the Master of
the Invincible Stand,

301
00:29:07,340 --> 00:29:11,017
the Hanged Man, he is
my precious dearest son.

302
00:29:11,100 --> 00:29:13,560
His name is J. Gaia!

303
00:29:41,100 --> 00:29:41,930
Let's go.

304
00:30:42,800 --> 00:30:44,200
Let's go.
